# BLOCKER carried to the lead: `SecureDesktopInstaller` (mixdog-tools desktop/computer_screen/installer.rs) is `pub(super)` inside the private module
# `computer_screen`, owned by s3-01a, so this domain cannot name it. The domain takes the trait `PcAccessInstaller` (state, install, enroll) instead.
# Needed in mixdog-tools (s3-01a's files, or the task that next owns computer_screen): a `pub` adapter implementing that trait over the one
# installer instance, mapping InstallState and KeyChangeOutcome 1:1 (Installed, Outdated, NotInstalled, NotEnrolled, OtherUser, Unavailable;
# Installed, Updated, Enrolled, Declined, Failed, InProgress, OtherUser, Unavailable, everything else `KeyOutcome::Other(<kebab-case name>)`),
# `install(keys, revoke)` = `SecureDesktopInstaller::install(keys, KeyChangeOptions { revoke, credential: None, delegated: None })`,
# `enroll` likewise, carrying `detail` and `exit_code`, and reachable from compose_flip.rs (for example `ComputerSessionPool::pc_access_installer()`).
